    EXTRACTION_PROMPT: `You are a meticulous medical records assistant. The person who uploaded this document is building their own complete personal health record, and NOTHING in the document may be left out. You are shown ONE uploaded document (it may be an after-visit summary, discharge paperwork, lab or imaging results, a medication list, a prescription, a referral, an appointment notice, a progress note, an insurance/benefits letter, a bill, or similar).

Read the ENTIRE document - every page, header, footer, table, sidebar, stamp, and handwritten note - and extract everything.

Respond with ONLY raw JSON (no markdown code fences, no commentary before or after) matching exactly this shape:

{
  "document": { "type": "", "title": "", "date": "", "time": "", "facility": "", "provider": "", "patientName": "", "pages": "" },
  "summary": "",
  "keyFindings": [ "" ],
  "doctors": [ { "title": "", "name": "", "specialty": "", "clinic": "", "address": "", "phone": "", "email": "" } ],
  "medications": [ { "name": "", "dose": "", "frequency": "", "route": "", "purpose": "", "purposeSource": "", "doctorName": "", "startDate": "", "lastFilledDate": "", "quantity": "", "refills": "", "instructions": "", "status": "" } ],
  "conditions": [ { "name": "", "icd10": "", "icd9": "", "date": "", "priority": "" } ],
  "allergies": [ { "name": "", "severity": "", "reaction": "" } ],
  "vitals": [ { "date": "", "time": "", "systolic": "", "diastolic": "", "heartRate": "", "spo2": "", "temp": "", "weight": "", "notes": "" } ],
  "labs": [ { "test": "", "result": "", "unit": "", "referenceRange": "", "flag": "", "date": "" } ],
  "procedures": [ { "name": "", "date": "", "result": "", "notes": "" } ],
  "instructions": [ "" ],
  "nextSteps": [ { "task": "", "category": "", "dueDate": "", "dueTime": "", "provider": "", "location": "", "notes": "" } ],
  "allOtherInformation": [ { "label": "", "value": "" } ]
}

Rules:
- COMPLETENESS IS REQUIRED. Every fact in the document must land somewhere in this JSON. Anything that does not fit a specific field (phone numbers, addresses, account/visit numbers, insurance details, billing amounts, codes, signatures, department names, contact instructions, disclaimers that contain instructions, etc.) goes into "allOtherInformation" as label/value pairs. Before answering, re-read the document and confirm nothing was skipped.
- "document.type" must be exactly one of: After-Visit Summary, Discharge Summary, Lab Results, Imaging Report, Prescription / Medication List, Referral, Appointment Notice, Progress Note, Insurance / Benefits, Letter / Correspondence, Billing Statement, Other.
- "document.date" is the date of service or the date the document was issued (YYYY-MM-DD). "document.time" is the visit/issue time in 24-hour HH:MM if shown, otherwise "".
- "summary" is a FULL-PAGE, plain-language summary (aim for 300-700 words; longer if the document is long). Cover: what the document is, who/when/where, the reason for the visit, what was found, every diagnosis, every medication and any change to it, every test result, every instruction, and every follow-up. Separate paragraphs with a blank line. Do not give medical advice beyond what the document says.
- "keyFindings": the most important points, one short sentence each.
- MEDICATIONS MUST ALWAYS HAVE A PURPOSE. If the document states why the medication is taken, use that and set "purposeSource" to "stated". If it does not, give the most likely reason based on the diagnoses in this document or the medication's standard use, and set "purposeSource" to "inferred". Never leave "purpose" blank. "status" is one of: new, continued, changed, stopped, unknown. "lastFilledDate" is the fill/dispense date if shown.
- All dates YYYY-MM-DD; all times 24-hour HH:MM. If the document gives a relative date (e.g. "follow up in 2 weeks"), calculate the actual date from the document date and keep the original wording in "notes".
- "nextSteps": every follow-up appointment, test or lab to schedule, referral, phone call to make, refill, paperwork, monitoring task, or instruction with a deadline. "category" must be exactly one of: Appointment, Lab / Test, Medication, Referral, Call / Contact, Paperwork, Self-Care, Other.
- For "doctors", "title" must be exactly one of: Dr., ARNP, PA-C, RN, Case Manager, Coordinator, Social Worker, Therapist, Other. Only use "Dr." for physicians. Include every provider, nurse, or staff member named with their contact details.
- For "allergies", "severity" must be exactly one of: Mild, Moderate, Severe, Anaphylaxis. If not stated, use "Moderate".
- "vitals": one entry per set of readings; numbers only (no units). Temperature in Fahrenheit (convert if needed).
- "labs": every test result row, including normal ones. "flag" is H, L, Abnormal, Critical, or "" if normal/not marked.
- Use an empty string "" for any field not present, and an empty array [] for any category with nothing. Do not invent values except the medication purpose rule above.
- Return raw JSON only, nothing else.`,

    getKey(){ try{ return safeStorage.getItem(this.configKey) || ''; } catch(e){ return ''; } },
    saveKey(){
      const inp = document.getElementById('ai-key-input');
      const val = inp ? inp.value.trim() : '';
      if(!val){ App.ui.toast('Enter a key first.', 'error'); return; }
      try{ safeStorage.setItem(this.configKey, val); } catch(e){ App.ui.toast('Could not save the key on this device.', 'error'); return; }
      if(inp) inp.value = '';
      App.ui.toast('API key saved on this device.');
      this.renderKeyStatus();
    },
    clearKey(){
      App.ui.confirmDialog('Remove the saved Anthropic API key from this device?').then(yes=>{
        if(!yes) return;
